  "id": "cable-pull-through",
  "name": "Cable Pull-Through",
  "definition": "A bilateral feet-planted low-pulley rope hip hinge facing away from the cable station, with the cable passing between the legs. Sussex Sport establishes the cable/rope topology, wide stance, slight knee bend, hip-back descent and upright hip-extension endpoint. Spine position held and straight passive elbows narrow the authored fixture as technique targets, not measured kinematics. Gluteus maximus is primary and medial hamstrings secondary by Arnold anatomy and resistance mechanics; lumbar extensors and abdominal regions stabilize the held trunk. The unsplit visible biceps-femoris region receives knee-control stabilizer credit only. No exact-fixture EMG, ranking or hypertrophy claim is made. Good mornings with dynamic spinal extension, floor pulls, squat-pulls, swings, shoulder raises, unilateral ankle-cuff kickbacks and band variants remain outside. Product weights are editable seeds, not source prescriptions. Brachialis receives categorical held-elbow control credit, without a dynamic elbow-flexion action.",
